  "limitations": [
    "Coarse batch resume recomputes unfinished successful work; recorded failures retry only explicitly.",
    "Output matrix buffering is bounded, with a one-window minimum; continuous EEG and estimator/packing caches are additional RAM.",
    "More small batches increase file count and fixed I/O cost; no universal optimal batch size claimed.",
    "No new seeding policy; stochastic recomputation after resume may differ.",
    "Resume verifies source size/mtime/header hash and declarations, not full-file checksums or a complete prior-payload scan.",
    "Uncatchable termination cannot provide final session wall time; resume records it as unknown.",
    "Composite reader supports ordinary NumPy time means; the existing packed mean helper targets individual production stores.",
    "Real tests use four contacts, three windows and five representative metrics per patient; not a full-patient/cohort benchmark or comprehensive mathematical validation.",
    "POSIX advisory locking; no automatic concurrency, parallelization, scientific corrections, custom referencing or separate data-lake/cache changes.",
    "Zarr async I/O stalled in the sandbox; integration/storage/real-data verification used approved execution outside it, writing only temporary output."
  ]
